==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*huspaz||derision, mockery}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hut-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hūt-||to be naughty, be impudent}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*kūd-||to mock}}. Related to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|hyspan||to mock, scorn, deride}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|hūsc||mockery, derision, scorn, insult}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|hosc||vilification, ridicule, scorn}}.

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hosp|m|hospas}}

# [[reproach]], [[contempt]], [[contumely]], [[insult]], [[blasphemy]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|hosp|}}

====Related terms====
* [[hospcwide]] m. insulting speech
* [[hospettan]] to ridicule
* [[hospspræc|hospsprǣċ]] f. jeer, taunt
* [[hospul]] contemptible
* [[hospword]] n. abusive language, contemptuous expression

